# Tailwind CSS v4 Conventions

## CSS Variable Shorthand

Tailwind v4 introduced a shorter syntax for referencing CSS custom properties.
Always use the shorthand form — never the legacy `[var(...)]` form:

```
# Wrong (Tailwind v3 style)
bg-[var(--antarctica-ink)]
text-[var(--antarctica-charcoal)]/40

# Correct (Tailwind v4 style)
bg-(--antarctica-ink)
text-(--antarctica-charcoal)/40
```

The pattern applies to **any** utility prefix: `bg-`, `text-`, `ring-`, `border-`,
`fill-`, `stroke-`, `shadow-`, `from-`, `via-`, `to-`, `accent-`, `caret-`, etc.

## Arbitrary Values vs Shorthand

| Scenario | Use |
|---|---|
| CSS variable | `bg-(--my-var)` |
| Arbitrary fixed value | `bg-[#1a2b3c]` or `bg-[24px]` |
| Arbitrary value with opacity | `bg-(--my-var)/50` |

## Responsive and State Variants

Variants compose normally with the shorthand:

```tsx
className="hover:text-(--antarctica-ice) lg:bg-(--antarctica-ink)"
```

## Project CSS Variables

All brand tokens are defined in `src/app/globals.css` under `:root`:

- `--antarctica-ink` — primary dark navy
- `--antarctica-ice` — brand teal/blue
- `--antarctica-ice-light` — lighter teal for progress track backgrounds
- `--antarctica-charcoal` — secondary text
- `--antarctica-line` — subtle border/ring colour
